# Implementation Plan - HOTFIX-010 — Keyboard Shortcuts for Overlay Opacity Control

Implement `Ctrl + Q` and `Ctrl + W` global application keyboard shortcuts to decrease and increase overlay opacity in 5% steps.

## Requirements & Semantics

> [!IMPORTANT]
> - **`Ctrl + Q`**: Decreases window opacity by 5% $\rightarrow$ UI Transparency $T = \min(100, \text{current} + 5)$.
> - **`Ctrl + W`**: Increases window opacity by 5% $\rightarrow$ UI Transparency $T = \max(0, \text{current} - 5)$.
> - Shortcuts must work application-wide regardless of focused child widget inside BatmanOverlay.
> - Slider, numeric display, Qt window opacity, and `ConfigManager` settings remain synchronized.

